# Adobe Creative Cloud — Photoshop Team Engineering Standards

## Code Quality
- TypeScript strict mode required across all packages
- All exported functions must have JSDoc comments with @param and @returns
- Use Zod for runtime input validation on all API routes
- Meaningful variable names — no single-letter variables outside loop iterators

## Security
- NEVER log PII, credentials, API keys, or file paths containing user data
- Image data must not persist in memory beyond the request lifecycle
- All file uploads must validate MIME type against an allowlist
- Sanitize all user-provided filenames before filesystem operations

## Error Handling
- All API endpoints must return structured error responses: { error: { code, message, details? } }
- All async operations must have explicit try/catch (no unhandled promise rejections)
- Use custom error classes that extend a base AppError

## Style
- camelCase for variables and functions, PascalCase for types and classes
- Barrel exports from each module's index.ts
- Prefer named exports over default exports